  "limitations": [
    "Native API time is synchronous host wall time, not GPU execution time. Remaining CPU time includes JS, instrumentation overhead and uncovered APIs, including GPUCanvasContext.getCurrentTexture.",
    "Only static 10k/1080p cases are measured here. This does not replace the broader 5k/10k static/moving benchmark or resolve known intermittent shading differences.",
    "The canonical pixel gate covers these final captures only. It does not establish temporal determinism or equal visual quality across different native render pipelines.",
    "Per-method p95 values cannot be added to form overall CPU p95. Mean method shares and the methods in an actual overall-p95 sample are retained instead.",
    "Browser performance.now quantization makes many individual fast-call samples zero. Pooled method means are observations at this clock resolution, not precise single-call latency estimates."
  ]
